    <MultiLanguageText Lang="de-DE" />
    <MultiLanguageText Lang="en-GB" />
    <MultiLanguageText Lang="en-US">
If the input value (x) is in the range of the dead zone (-zoneBorder &lt; x &lt; + zoneBorder), the output value is set to zero.
If the input value is at / below (–zoneBorder) or at / above +zoneBorder, input x is the output value.
The dead zone – symmetrical around the zero point – can be set using the value zoneBorder.

| Input value x                    | Return value   |
| -------------------------------- | -------------- |
| x &lt;= -zoneBorder                 | x              |
| -zoneBorder &lt; x &lt; zoneBorder     | 0              |
| x &gt;= zoneBorder                  | x              |

![Zone border fitler](DeadZone.png)

</MultiLanguageText>
